#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:16
msgid "Video 12: millis Function 丨 Handling Multiple Tasks 丨 Non-Blocking Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:18
msgid "This tutorial dives into the essentials of implementing non-blocking code using the millis() function in Arduino programming, demonstrated through controlling a Servo motor and a traffic light operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:20
msgid "**Non-blocking Code**: Explains the importance of using millis() instead of delay() for timing events in Arduino."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:21
msgid "**Millis Function**: Demonstrates how the millis() function can be used to keep track of time and perform tasks without blocking code execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:22
msgid "**Servo Motor Control**: Shows how to control a Servo motor using non-blocking code to achieve smooth motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:23
msgid "**LED Blinking**: Illustrates how to make an LED blink at regular intervals without using delay()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:24
msgid "**Button Input**: Demonstrates how to handle button input in a non-blocking manner to trigger events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:25
msgid "**Simultaneous Tasks**: Guides through managing multiple tasks simultaneously, creating an illusion of multitasking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_12_millis_Function.rst:26
msgid "**Challenge Activity**: Modify the program to create a traffic light system with a barrier controlled by a Servo motor, including an emergency button for pedestrians."
msgstr ""

